-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why GPLv3
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
infraCFD uses the Gmsh Python API (`import gmsh`) for mesh generation. Gmsh is
licensed under the GNU GPL (v2 or later), and linking against its API makes the
combined work subject to the GPL. GPLv3 is compatible with both Gmsh and
OpenFOAM (GPLv3), so infraCFD is released under GPLv3.

(OpenFOAM is invoked as a separate external program via subprocess, which is
arm's-length use; the GPL obligation on infraCFD itself stems primarily from the
Gmsh Python binding.)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- OpenFOAM (solver, external)        — GPLv3        — https://www.openfoam.com
- Gmsh (meshing, Python API)         — GPLv2+       — https://gmsh.info
- Three.js (3D viewer)               — MIT          — https://threejs.org
- FastAPI / Starlette / uvicorn      — MIT / BSD    — backend
- trimesh                            — MIT          — GLB/STL handling
- NumPy, SciPy                       — BSD          — numerics

These dependencies are NOT redistributed with infraCFD; install them separately
(see README).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Example data & models
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- 2D/3D test cases (cfd-testcases.js): cross-section and building geometries
  derived from the SOFiSTiK "Dolfyn" CFD example library
  (https://www.sofistik.com). Reference coefficient values are quoted from the
  respective published benchmarks / wind-tunnel data for validation only.
- DFG benchmark (Schäfer & Turek, 1996): laminar cylinder-in-channel reference.
- CesiumMan example model: © Cesium GS, Inc., licensed CC-BY 4.0
  (https://github.com/CesiumGS/cesium). Included only as a demo GLB.

Do not redistribute third-party example geometries or models without verifying
their respective licenses.
